Yes, you can use the `rle` function in R, which stands for "run length encoding". This function identifies runs or sequences of identical values and returns a list with the lengths of these runs and the values themselves. However, to adapt it to your needs, you can create a custom function that uses `rle` to identify the start and end of continuous sequences. Here's how you can do it:

```R
find_intervals <- function(vec) {
  rle_data <- rle(vec)
  intervals <- list()

  for (i in seq_along(rle_data$lengths)) {
    start <- vec[which(rle_data$values[i] == min(vec[rle_data$values == rle_data$values[i]]))]
    end <- vec[which(rle_data$values[i] == max(vec[rle_data$values == rle_data$values[i]]))]
    intervals[[paste0("interval", i+1)]] <- c(start, end)
  }

  intervals
}

