samples.guided_completion:
No, modules do not prevent the need to use the DOMContentLoaded event. Modules are executed as soon as they are ready, which is before the DOMContentLoaded event. If your module needs to access the DOM, you will still need to wait for the DOM to be fully loaded.

However, you can use the import() function to import modules asynchronously and wait for the DOM to be loaded:

import('my-module.js')
.then(module => {
  // The DOM is now fully loaded
  document.querySelector('my-element').addEventListener('click', () => {
    // ...
  });
});

This way, the module is only imported and executed after the DOMContentLoaded event has been fired.

