return $parent && $parent.length ? $parent : $this.parent()

I am not able to grasp the above line completely, I understand Logical And (&&) and the Ternary Conditional Operator (... ? ... : ...), but I don't seem to comprehend how they interact in the above example. Now if I add a console.log before the return statement:

console.log($parent && $parent.length ? $parent : $this.parent());

I get:

Object { 0: <li.dropdown.open>, length: 1, prevObject: Object, context: <a.dropdown-toggle>, selector: ".parent()" }

Which indeed is $this.parent()

