samples.guided_completion:
The problem is that you are not null-terminating the string. When you print the string, the printf function will keep printing characters until it finds a null character. If the string is not null-terminated, printf will keep printing whatever is in memory after the string. This is why you get undefined characters.

To fix this, you should add a null character at the end of the string:

new_str[i] = str[len - 1 - i];
new_str[len] = '\0';

Alternatively, you can initialize the string with a null character before the loop:

memset(new_str, 0, N);

or you can use an array of size N+1 and make sure the last element is always 0:

