We are using Spark 2.x with Scala for a system that has 13 different ETL operations. 7 of them are relatively simple and each driven by a single domain class, and differ primarily by this class and some nuances in how the load is handled. A simplified version of the load class is as follows, for the purposes of this example say that there are 7 pizza toppings being loaded, here's Pepperoni:

object LoadPepperoni {
